  // ================= feat_talks (owner, Oct 29): TOOLBOX TALKS =================
  // Tools › Toolbox Talks. The library (talks.json + mental_health.json, fact-checked, used as written) is inert JSON in
  // <script type="application/json" id="pbTalksLib">, parsed the first time a talk is needed (never at start-up).
  // Everyone with Tools can read it. A FOREMAN also has: a schedule (weekdays; every week or every 2 weeks; default
  // Monday), a queue (add / reorder / remove), "Pick one at random" (never a talk he gave in the last N months until the
  // library runs out), "Mark as given" (date, job = his Current job, the crew who were there). Everything is kept on this
  // phone first (<uid>:pbTalks) and sent when there is signal (sql/73: pb_talk_plan_set, pb_talk_give, pb_talk_mine).
  // His Home shows "Toolbox talk today: <title>" on a due day until one is given; the server pushes the same morning.
  // The office (company account, managers, PMs, supers) reads the talks given per job (pb_talks_office).
